    "summary": "Punta Rocas is an exposed reef break in Punta Negra, about 45 km south of Lima, and one of Peru's best-known contest venues. It is mainly a right-hander, with a left on some swells, and it handles serious size, from about 3 ft up to 15 ft. The best waves come on south-southwest groundswells, usually from April to October, with offshore winds from the east. It is often crowded, and surfers need to watch for rips and rocks.",
