   "spot_text": {
    "summary": "Punta Roca is El Salvador's most famous wave: a fast, hollow right-hand point break that runs over cobblestones and black boulders under the headland at La Libertad, about 20 minutes from San Salvador airport. Long-period south swells wrap around the point and can link sections for up to several hundred metres. The takeoff at the top (La Punta) is steep and shallow, and the wave is best suited to experienced surfers. Surfertoday compares it to South Africa's Jeffreys Bay.",
