   "spot_text": {
    "summary": "El Sunzal is a long, consistent right-hand point break next to Playa El Tunco on El Salvador's coast. It breaks in deep water, picks up almost every swell, and peels for around 250 yards with open carving walls rather than barrels. That makes it one of the most consistent waves in the country, with gentler waves for learning from November to February and long, powerful rides on bigger southwest swells.",
